    "angle": 0,
    "content": "where  \\( T_{q} \\)  is the Hecke operator and  \\( \\zeta_{\\mathfrak{q}}(s):=\\prod_{v|\\mathfrak{q}}\\zeta_{F_{v}}(s) \\)  is the partial Dedekind zeta function. If the integral ideal q is squarefree, i.e. m=1, we define  \\( T_{q_{1}^{m-2}}:=0 \\)  and  \\( \\lambda_{\\pi_{2}}\\left(\\mathfrak{q}_{1}^{m-2}\\right):=0 \\) . Hence,  \\( T_{q_{1}^{m-2}}\\varphi_{2}=0 \\) . Moreover, the degree of the Hecke operator  \\( T_{l} \\)  is defined by",
    "merge_prev": false
